How was her speaking before?

234
00:19:10.571 --> 00:19:12.039
Just normal.

235
00:19:12.222 --> 00:19:13.874
Any physiological?

236
00:19:13.898 --> 00:19:15.944
Not a thing.

237
00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:18.071
Thought you might be interested.

238
00:19:18.856 --> 00:19:20.490
Definitely.

239
00:19:21.799 --> 00:19:22.977
Good.

240
00:19:26.096 --> 00:19:28.711
Which one's your favorite?

241
00:19:29.397 --> 00:19:31.161
You can just point.

242
00:19:32.708 --> 00:19:36.684
I like the cat.
But that's just me.

243
00:19:41.315 --> 00:19:44.232
Lucy, I know you're scared.

244
00:19:46.909 --> 00:19:51.457
But you're in a really
safe place, okay?

245
00:19:51.481 --> 00:19:54.281
And I wanna be here to help you.

246
00:19:54.307 --> 00:19:55.839
I promise you that.

247
00:20:02.269 --> 00:20:04.375
I...

248
00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:07.076
<font color="#D900D9">(EXHALES DEEPLY)</font>

249
00:20:07.076 --> 00:20:08.574
...don't love.

250
00:20:08.598 --> 00:20:10.855
<font color="#808080">THERAPIST:</font>
But you have loved.

251
00:20:11.665 --> 00:20:14.026
Yeah, a long time ago once.

252
00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:16.940
So you know that you can love?

253
00:20:19.071 --> 00:20:21.218
I'm... There's nothing in here.
There's nothing.

254
00:20:21.242 --> 00:20:25.152
It's like... It's an empty well.
It's...

255
00:20:25.176 --> 00:20:27.597
just dry and barren.

256
00:20:28.414 --> 00:20:32.208
Is that why you sleep with all these men?

257
00:20:32.374 --> 00:20:35.092
- No.
- So what is it you want?

258
00:20:35.116 --> 00:20:36.750
- I don't want anything.
- Well, you must want something,

259
00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.519
you continue to do it.

260
00:20:39.049 --> 00:20:40.288
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

261
00:20:40.289 --> 00:20:42.529
<font color="#808080">THERAPIST:</font>
So how does it make you feel?

262
00:20:42.555 --> 00:20:43.945
- Happy?
- No.

263
00:20:43.971 --> 00:20:45.420
Pretty?

264
00:20:45.444 --> 00:20:47.666
- No!
- So what?

265
00:20:48.403 --> 00:20:50.930
It makes me feel...

266
00:20:52.666 --> 00:20:57.749
It makes me feel... something,

267
00:20:57.773 --> 00:20:59.950
because most of the time
I feel nothing.

268
00:20:59.974 --> 00:21:03.349
And these are men that
you don't even like.

269
00:21:03.375 --> 00:21:04.702
Right.

270
00:21:05.384 --> 00:21:09.500
So what would you do if you met a man
that you actually did like?

271
00:21:09.525 --> 00:21:11.064
I don't know.

272
00:21:12.721 --> 00:21:16.854
Probably make him regret the day
he laid eyes on me.

273
00:21:17.105 --> 00:21:19.230
<font color="#D900D9">(MUSIC PLAYING)</font>

274
00:21:20.676 --> 00:21:21.821
<font color="#808080">BRIAN:</font> Hey.

275
00:21:21.846 --> 00:21:24.479
How are you doing?
What's your name?

276
00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:25.714
Katie.

277
00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.787
Katie, I'm Brian.
Nice to meet you.

278
00:21:28.811 --> 00:21:30.650
You study here? I think I've seen
you around before.

279
00:21:30.651 --> 00:21:31.519
Yeah.

280
00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.445
- Awesome. What are you studying?
- Psychology.

281
00:21:33.471 --> 00:21:35.003
No way!
I got a buddy over there..

282
00:21:35.005 --> 00:21:37.519
who's just shooting pools
also studying psychology.

283
00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.615
I just took an intro course once.
I love that shit, it's like... pooh.

284
00:21:40.641 --> 00:21:41.654
You know.

285
00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.758
<font color="#D900D9">(BOTH CHUCKLES)</font>

286
00:21:43.759 --> 00:21:45.469
So what are you drinking?
A Beer?

287
00:21:45.493 --> 00:21:47.227
Can I get you a drink?

288
00:21:47.251 --> 00:21:48.273
I may get you a drink.

289
00:21:48.298 --> 00:21:50.827
Hey, can we get two beers,
One for me, one for Katie over here?

290
00:21:50.853 --> 00:21:52.298
- <font color="#808080">BARTENDER:</font> Got you.
- Thanks.

291
00:21:53.789 --> 00:21:55.007
So...

292
00:21:55.031 --> 00:21:56.306
Hmm.

293
00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:58.188
- Three beers already, Katie.
- <font color="#D900D9">(KATIE SCOFFS)</font>

294
00:21:58.494 --> 00:22:00.721
Brian, you must be a math major.

295
00:22:01.583 --> 00:22:03.354
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLES)</font>
That's good, that's good.

296
00:22:04.865 --> 00:22:07.647
So tell me Katie,
what's your story?

297
00:22:07.673 --> 00:22:13.749
Well, Brian, I have very
self-destructive tendencies.

298
00:22:14.049 --> 00:22:16.500
- <font color="#D900D9">(KATIE GASPS, MOANING)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(BRIAN MAONS, GROANS)</font>

299
00:22:18.099 --> 00:22:20.414
<font color="#D900D9">(TELEPHONE RINGING)</font>

300
00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:25.299
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font> Hello...

301
00:22:25.315 --> 00:22:27.299
- <font color="#808080">TIM:</font> William.
- Hey, Tim.

302
00:22:28.099 --> 00:22:30.299
Thank you, sir.

303
00:22:33.705 --> 00:22:35.548
- Jake.
- William.

304
00:22:35.573 --> 00:22:37.896
- Scotch, neat.
- Right away, sir.

305
00:22:39.519 --> 00:22:44.422
Elizabeth can be difficult.
Nobody knows that better than I do.

306
00:22:45.049 --> 00:22:47.207
<font color="#D900D9">(WILLIAM SIGHS)</font>

307
00:22:47.208 --> 00:22:49.536
Jake, it hasn't been two years
since she lost her sister.

308
00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:52.699
I mean, they were very close.

309
00:22:53.388 --> 00:22:55.559
Tricia hated Elizabeth.

310
00:22:55.912 --> 00:22:58.512
Well, sisters sometimes say things...

311
00:22:58.538 --> 00:23:02.278
Out-of-controlling, selfish, judgemental.

312
00:23:02.303 --> 00:23:05.395
Yeah. Okay. Right. Well, listen,
we're both fairly bright guys.

313
00:23:05.421 --> 00:23:07.192
Let's just be frank.

314
00:23:08.375 --> 00:23:10.319
We proposed something that
you've got us know you had no interest.

315
00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:12.748
I'm not gonna bring that up again.

316
00:23:12.749 --> 00:23:15.994
But the reason
I asked you here today is...

317
00:23:16.019 --> 00:23:17.159
Thank you.

318
00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:22.993
Worthington called me, and they said
you're planning to pull Katie out of the school.

319
00:23:23.019 --> 00:23:24.634
Well, that's a mistake.

320
00:23:24.894 --> 00:23:29.128
I mean, if there's a better girl's school in
the country, that'd be news to me.

321
00:23:29.153 --> 00:23:30.807
I simply can't afford it.

322
00:23:30.833 --> 00:23:34.653
Please, that's our pleasure.
You're never gonna see a bill.

323
00:23:34.677 --> 00:23:38.856
I promise.
It's the least we can do.

324
00:23:39.257 --> 00:23:41.322
You've done enough already.

325
00:23:41.346 --> 00:23:45.122
Well, the public schools are a jungle.
Is that what you want for Katie?

326
00:23:45.146 --> 00:23:46.608
I'll figure something out.

327
00:23:46.634 --> 00:23:48.807
Well, like what?
There's public and there's private.

328
00:23:48.833 --> 00:23:50.855
Those are the options.

329
00:23:52.654 --> 00:23:54.388
You all right?

330
00:23:55.005 --> 00:23:56.897
I mean that...

331
00:23:56.923 --> 00:24:01.267
You know how difficult it is to get a kid
into a good private school in New York?

332
00:24:01.291 --> 00:24:05.623
Everybody's rich that applies,
and they're connected and underhanded.

333
00:24:06.665 --> 00:24:09.174
I'll figure something out.
Let me buy you a drink.

334
00:24:09.200 --> 00:24:11.424
- You'll not...
- Jake.

335
00:24:12.069 --> 00:24:15.982
You'll not be raising
my daughter by committing.

336
00:24:58.049 --> 00:25:00.119
<font color="#D900D9">(SIRENS WALING IN DISTANT)</font>

337
00:25:11.049 --> 00:25:13.230
<font color="#D900D9">(HORNS HONKING IN DISTANT)</font>

338
00:25:28.804 --> 00:25:30.907
You like my bike?

339
00:25:31.625 --> 00:25:34.757
I used to have a pink bike
when I was a little girl.

340
00:25:36.094 --> 00:25:38.217
Do you know how to ride?

341
00:25:38.241 --> 00:25:40.481
Do you know how to ride a bike?

342
00:25:41.590 --> 00:25:44.375
Do any of your friends have bikes?

343
00:25:50.832 --> 00:25:54.767
If you want, one day I can take you out
and teach you how to ride.

344
00:25:54.791 --> 00:25:59.165
We could go out to the park
one of these days.

345
00:26:01.093 --> 00:26:02.750
It could be fun.

346
00:26:05.584 --> 00:26:08.056
So how's it going with Lucy?
She talking?

347
00:26:08.080 --> 00:26:09.641
It's a process.

348
00:26:09.665 --> 00:26:11.269
So she's not talking.

349
00:26:11.295 --> 00:26:14.500
Look, I'm going to transfer
the case to Dr. Weinberg,

350
00:26:14.500 --> 00:26:16.083
she's a very experienced
psychologist.

351
00:26:16.084 --> 00:26:18.051
I just need more time.

352
00:26:18.076 --> 00:26:21.442
And I need something to put
into her sixty-day report.

353
00:26:21.803 --> 00:26:26.200
Look, this isn't about trying
to impress the state agency

354
00:26:26.201 --> 00:26:29.353
that just so happens to fund us
at a time of severe cutbacks.

355
00:26:29.354 --> 00:26:31.375
It's about helping this little girl...

356
00:26:31.375 --> 00:26:33.398
who's suffered such severe trauma
she can't even speak anymore,

357
00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:38.357
and will live an unbearably bleak life
if we don't connect with her, and soon.

358
00:26:39.166 --> 00:26:42.471
Now we've failed her,
and we have to fix it.

359
00:26:42.497 --> 00:26:44.541
We've not failed her.

360
00:26:44.567 --> 00:26:47.569
Katie, you're a very
bright young woman.

361
00:26:47.595 --> 00:26:50.967
You're gonna be an exceptional
psychologist someday.

362
00:26:50.991 --> 00:26:54.279
But you need to know when
to admit defeat, and move on.

363
00:26:54.305 --> 00:26:56.856
Let me take her to the park, okay?

364
00:26:56.882 --> 00:27:01.923
- I think a different environment should just...
- There's no environment, as therapist.

365
00:27:02.207 --> 00:27:06.999
You know we can't let you take her off grounds.
But you got your week.

366
00:27:08.790 --> 00:27:09.616
Thanks.

367
00:27:09.642 --> 00:27:11.737
Katie? A week is a week!

368
00:27:11.761 --> 00:27:12.971
Yep.

369
00:27:14.005 --> 00:27:16.519
- <font color="#D900D9">(DOOR CLOSES)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)</font>

370
00:27:26.999 --> 00:27:29.328
- Jake! Hi.
- Hey.

371
00:27:29.354 --> 00:27:31.652
Ah, it is so good to see you again.

372
00:27:31.676 --> 00:27:34.038
- Pleased to meet you again.
- Yeah, of course, of course.

373
00:27:34.064 --> 00:27:35.530
Why don't you come on back?

374
00:27:35.556 --> 00:27:39.390
I just wanna tell you again
how sorry we all are about Patricia.

375
00:27:39.414 --> 00:27:43.583
That was a... It was just a
big loss for our whole community.

376
00:27:43.888 --> 00:27:45.385
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

377
00:27:45.411 --> 00:27:47.304
How's Katie doing?

378
00:27:47.328 --> 00:27:49.059
- She's fine.
- Yeah?

379
00:27:49.092 --> 00:27:51.628
When she left Copen, she moved in
with her aunt and uncle?

380
00:27:51.653 --> 00:27:52.480
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

381
00:27:52.505 --> 00:27:55.373
- But she's back with me now.
- Oh, good, good.

382
00:27:55.642 --> 00:28:00.163
And, uh... I would really like her
to come back to Copen.

383
00:28:00.188 --> 00:28:02.369
Well, it's the middle of the year,
you know.

384
00:28:02.394 --> 00:28:04.650
Do you really think pulling her out of
Worthington is the best thing right now?

385
00:28:04.674 --> 00:28:06.223
I already did.

386
00:28:06.249 --> 00:28:09.557
Oh! Uh... Gosh!

387
00:28:09.583 --> 00:28:12.085
Look, Jake you know we would really love
to have Katie back with us,

388
00:28:12.109 --> 00:28:15.221
but... we're completely full.

389
00:28:16.040 --> 00:28:18.207
Always room for one more.

390
00:28:18.231 --> 00:28:20.531
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font> Ah, it's just, um...

391
00:28:20.557 --> 00:28:21.557
I'm sorry.

392
00:28:21.582 --> 00:28:23.194
What about faculty?

393
00:28:23.220 --> 00:28:25.829
- What about them?
- The faculty get priority for admission.

394
00:28:25.855 --> 00:28:27.650
Ah, yes and free to...

395
00:28:27.674 --> 00:28:31.184
I will teach creative writing
for seniors.

396
00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:33.460
Ah, okay. Well, I don't think we're
budgeted for something like that.

397
00:28:33.484 --> 00:28:34.958
For a dollar a semester.

398
00:28:34.982 --> 00:28:37.218
Jake, I appreciate it,
I really do.

399
00:28:37.250 --> 00:28:38.861
Um, the craft of short story?

400
00:28:38.885 --> 00:28:43.843
We'll focus on student work,
study of the masters,

401
00:28:43.867 --> 00:28:46.334
Twain, Hemingway, Roth and...

402
00:28:46.358 --> 00:28:48.852
maybe a piece
I'm currently working on.

403
00:28:48.876 --> 00:28:51.359
Okay, you really wanna teach
creative writing to 12th graders?

404
00:28:51.384 --> 00:28:55.163
I really want my daughter
to go to Copen.

405
00:28:55.511 --> 00:28:57.806
And you'd write recommendations
for the college applications?

406
00:28:57.830 --> 00:29:01.557
If any student shows,
then talent them.

407
00:29:01.583 --> 00:29:05.531
Talent being generously defined.

408
00:29:16.875 --> 00:29:18.689
Katie can start next week.

409
00:29:20.069 --> 00:29:21.766
Can you start next semester?

410
00:29:21.790 --> 00:29:23.365
I can indeed.

411
00:29:26.229 --> 00:29:27.583
Thank you.

412
00:29:28.223 --> 00:29:30.744
Do you know what my
favorite part of the day is?

413
00:29:30.769 --> 00:29:34.691
- What?
- This part, taking you to school.

414
00:29:36.089 --> 00:29:38.420
<font color="#D900D9">(CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)</font>

415
00:29:49.099 --> 00:29:51.619
<font color="#D900D9">(TELEPHONE RINGING)</font>

416
00:29:52.290 --> 00:29:53.628
I'm working.

417
00:30:04.472 --> 00:30:05.727
Hello?

418
00:30:05.751 --> 00:30:08.147
<font color="#808080">ELIZABETH:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(ON PHONE)</font>
Hi, Jake, it's Elizabeth calling.

419
00:30:09.354 --> 00:30:10.854
Hey, Elizabeth.

420
00:30:11.915 --> 00:30:13.031
Hi. Um...

421
00:30:13.712 --> 00:30:17.315
I'm calling to invite you and Katie
over for dinner.

422
00:30:17.960 --> 00:30:19.881
What day would work for you?

423
00:30:19.882 --> 00:30:22.573
<font color="#D900D9">(STAMMERING)</font>
How does Thursday sound?

424
00:30:22.597 --> 00:30:25.215
Uh, no. Look,
Thursday I'm on a writer's panel.

425
00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:26.634
What about Saturday?

426
00:30:26.659 --> 00:30:29.459
Dottie's making her meatloaf,
it's Katie favorite.

427
00:30:29.483 --> 00:30:31.224
Yeah? Oh, she would love that.

428
00:30:31.250 --> 00:30:33.269
You know, but Saturday, you see,
we're going to the park,

429
00:30:33.270 --> 00:30:35.720
she's gonna get
really tired afterwards.

430
00:30:36.445 --> 00:30:40.179
Listen Jake, stop playing games
with me, all right?

431
00:30:40.707 --> 00:30:43.628
Katie lived with us for a year.

432
00:30:43.804 --> 00:30:47.986
The boys miss her terribly,
as do William and I.

433
00:30:48.290 --> 00:30:51.324
Now are you going to come
to dinner or not?

434
00:30:51.348 --> 00:30:52.647
I said yes.

435
00:30:52.673 --> 00:30:56.971
All right then, we should set a date
that works for you.

436
00:30:56.997 --> 00:30:58.523
Hey...

437
00:30:58.548 --> 00:31:01.780
Elizabeth, look, I'm writing at the moment.
Can I call you back? Thanks.

438
00:31:03.049 --> 00:31:05.230
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

439
00:31:19.618 --> 00:31:20.882
Come in.

440
00:31:21.163 --> 00:31:23.578
- Hey.
- Well, hey there.

441
00:31:25.884 --> 00:31:28.140
I have a gift for you.

442
00:31:29.247 --> 00:31:31.282
But that's not necessary.

443
00:31:36.038 --> 00:31:41.038
You didn't think I spent the whole time
in the hospital basket-living, did you?

444
00:31:41.602 --> 00:31:43.465
Bitter Tulips?

445
00:31:45.400 --> 00:31:48.718
Hmm. I like it.

446
00:31:49.500 --> 00:31:51.560
Any good?

447
00:31:51.586 --> 00:31:53.255
Best thing I've ever written.

448
00:31:53.279 --> 00:31:56.041
- Really?
- Mm-hmm. I'm sure of it.

449
00:31:56.099 --> 00:31:58.180
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLING)</font>

450
00:31:58.185 --> 00:32:00.150
You son of a gun!

451
00:32:00.394 --> 00:32:02.452
I'm gonna get this sold by lunch.

452
00:32:02.478 --> 00:32:05.959
Good, because I'm broke.
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)</font>

453
00:32:08.113 --> 00:32:11.520
<font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> I thought it'd be nice
to take a break from the office.

454
00:32:11.546 --> 00:32:14.405
Sit here and watch the ducks
go about their day?

455
00:32:16.049 --> 00:32:18.519
<font color="#D900D9">(DUCKS QUACKING)</font>

456
00:32:19.563 --> 00:32:23.719
In my next life,
I wanna come back as a duck.

457
00:32:25.123 --> 00:32:27.749
You can fly, you can swim.

458
00:32:29.539 --> 00:32:31.452
You can quack.

459
00:32:36.288 --> 00:32:38.080
Pretty nice.

460
00:32:57.209 --> 00:33:00.633
She sat there and held my hand.

461
00:33:00.657 --> 00:33:02.832
She held my hand.

462
00:33:02.856 --> 00:33:04.721
Where did this happen?

463
00:33:04.747 --> 00:33:06.506
In my office.

464
00:33:06.845 --> 00:33:10.445
- But... she didn't speak?
- No.

465
00:33:10.471 --> 00:33:12.497
So I'm transferring her
to Dr. Weinberg.

466
00:33:13.684 --> 00:33:16.436
- We are on the verge.
- What does "on the verge" mean?

467
00:33:16.461 --> 00:33:18.006
A week? A month?
A year? What?

468
00:33:18.030 --> 00:33:20.171
It means that we are
making progress.

469
00:33:20.195 --> 00:33:21.749
I'm sorry, Katie.

470
00:33:22.179 --> 00:33:24.686
- That's not fair!
- It's completely fair.

471
00:33:24.711 --> 00:33:28.538
Now you're to inform Lucy
that Tuesday's session will be your last.

472
00:33:28.563 --> 00:33:33.218
And at the end of the session, Dr. Weinberg
will come in and introduce herself.

473
00:33:33.242 --> 00:33:35.336
We're done here.

474
00:33:40.624 --> 00:33:43.432
Will you please put this back
on the shelf?

475
00:33:45.031 --> 00:33:46.142
Thank you.

476
00:33:49.049 --> 00:33:51.319
<font color="#D900D9">(KATIE INHALES, EXHALES)</font>

477
00:33:52.108 --> 00:33:57.525
Um... Lucy, I've had the best
couple of months with you.

478
00:33:58.005 --> 00:34:01.023
Oh boy! It's been such a pleasure
to get to know you,

479
00:34:01.048 --> 00:34:05.798
and to read, and play
and draw pictures.

480
00:34:08.233 --> 00:34:12.230
It's been so fun that I told my friend Carla
who works here, she's super nice,

481
00:34:12.231 --> 00:34:13.865
how much fun it's been.

482
00:34:13.867 --> 00:34:18.326
And she want's to play with you too.
So she's excited to meet you.

483
00:34:18.327 --> 00:34:22.556
She's actually gonna come by
in a couple of minutes to say, Hi.

484
00:34:22.581 --> 00:34:28.039
And... next time you come here, you're
gonna hang out with her, instead of me.

485
00:34:31.206 --> 00:34:32.655
No.

486
00:34:38.081 --> 00:34:40.597
I wanna stay with you.

487
00:34:46.099 --> 00:34:48.320
<font color="#D900D9">(CHILDREN SHRIEKING,
SHOUTING)</font>

488
00:34:54.780 --> 00:34:58.367
<font color="#808080">YOUNG KATIE:</font>
Daddy! Daddy!

489
00:34:59.137 --> 00:35:00.630
Daddy!

490
00:35:02.802 --> 00:35:03.925
- <font color="#808080">JAKE:</font> Hey!
- <font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> Hi!

491
00:35:03.951 --> 00:35:05.300
How are you doing?

492
00:35:05.326 --> 00:35:06.989
- I've got some great news.
- What?

493
00:35:07.014 --> 00:35:09.199
Daddy sold a book today.

494
00:35:09.224 --> 00:35:11.777
- Is that good?
- Is that good? Are you kidding me!

495
00:35:11.802 --> 00:35:13.623
It's the greatest news in the world!

496
00:35:13.648 --> 00:35:17.746
That means you can have any toy
on the entire planet.

497
00:35:18.123 --> 00:35:20.675
- I want a bike, pink with a basket and bell,
- A bike! Pink! Basket!

498
00:35:20.701 --> 00:35:22.987
- and streamers dangling from the handlebar.
- Those streamers, Okay!

499
00:35:23.012 --> 00:35:26.110
Let's go and get that!
That's what you should have!

500
00:35:27.289 --> 00:35:30.548
Keep your balance.
Keep your balance by looking forward.

501
00:35:30.940 --> 00:35:32.311
That's it!

502
00:35:32.335 --> 00:35:33.931
You're going great!

503
00:35:33.956 --> 00:35:36.641
It's all you. It's all you!

504
00:35:36.666 --> 00:35:38.173
Now accelerate.

505
00:35:38.434 --> 00:35:39.784
Here you go!

506
00:35:39.809 --> 00:35:42.340
Here you go. Keep your eyes up!
Keep looking where you're going.

507
00:35:42.365 --> 00:35:43.672
That's my girl!

508
00:35:43.697 --> 00:35:45.867
Oh, yeah!
She's got it.

509
00:35:45.891 --> 00:35:47.429
She's got it!

510
00:35:47.454 --> 00:35:48.846
Go, Katie!

511
00:35:52.083 --> 00:35:53.576
Go faster!

512
00:35:55.007 --> 00:35:57.166
Go, Katie!

513
00:35:58.079 --> 00:36:00.150
That's my girl!

514
00:36:03.224 --> 00:36:09.405
<font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(SING-ALONG)</font>
♪ Why do birds suddenly appear ♪

515
00:36:09.431 --> 00:36:15.125
♪ Every time you are near? ♪

516
00:36:15.150 --> 00:36:20.438
♪ Just like me, they long to be ♪

517
00:36:20.463 --> 00:36:24.536
♪ Close to you ♪

518
00:36:24.561 --> 00:36:30.969
<font color="#808080">KATIE & JAKE:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(SING-ALONG)</font>
♪ Why do stars fall down from the sky ♪

519
00:36:30.996 --> 00:36:36.737
♪ Every time you walk by? ♪

520
00:36:36.762 --> 00:36:42.202
♪ Just like me, they long to be ♪

521
00:36:42.228 --> 00:36:46.217
♪ Close to you ♪

522
00:36:47.675 --> 00:36:52.686
♪ On the day that you were
born the angels got together ♪

523
00:36:52.711 --> 00:36:57.780
♪ And decided to create
a dream come true ♪

524
00:36:57.804 --> 00:37:00.911
♪ So they sprinkled moon dust
in your hair ♪

525
00:37:00.936 --> 00:37:05.731
♪ And golden starlight
in your eyes of blue ♪

526
00:37:06.005 --> 00:37:08.175
<font color="#D900D9">(KATIE MAKES PIANO SOUNDS)</font>

527
00:37:08.177 --> 00:37:14.208
♪ That is why all
the girls in town ♪

528
00:37:14.233 --> 00:37:16.545
♪ Follow you all around ♪

529
00:37:16.570 --> 00:37:18.018
What are you writing?

530
00:37:18.043 --> 00:37:20.389
I am writing a new book.

531
00:37:20.414 --> 00:37:22.643
What's it about?

532
00:37:23.097 --> 00:37:24.318
It's about you.

533
00:37:24.344 --> 00:37:25.076
Me?

534
00:37:25.101 --> 00:37:26.101
Mm-hmm.

535
00:37:27.436 --> 00:37:31.407
I've called her Potato Chip
for as long as I can remember.

536
00:37:31.431 --> 00:37:33.809
I've no reason why I like the name.

537
00:37:41.318 --> 00:37:43.896
What do you think?
You like it?

538
00:37:43.920 --> 00:37:46.485
Could it be about us instead?

539
00:37:46.510 --> 00:37:49.164
- Can it be about us?
- Yeah.

540
00:37:51.489 --> 00:37:55.471
You know, kiddo, you are a genius!

541
00:37:55.969 --> 00:37:59.302
- My daughter is a genius!
- <font color="#D900D9">(KATIE GIGGLES)</font>

542
00:38:01.420 --> 00:38:03.007
Yeah, it can be about us.

543
00:38:03.032 --> 00:38:05.460
♪ So they sprinkled moon dust
in your hair ♪

544
00:38:05.485 --> 00:38:10.550
♪ And golden starlight
in your eyes of blue ♪

545
00:38:11.119 --> 00:38:14.320
<font color="#D900D9">(DISCO MUSIC PLAYING)</font>

546
00:38:21.306 --> 00:38:22.302
Hey.

547
00:38:23.206 --> 00:38:24.163
You know...

548
00:38:24.188 --> 00:38:28.012
Normally I would never approach
someone like you, but...

549
00:38:28.036 --> 00:38:30.061
I heard a rumor.

550
00:38:30.719 --> 00:38:32.259
What rumor?

551
00:38:32.284 --> 00:38:38.139
Um... That my literary idol and
your father are the same person.

552
00:38:38.590 --> 00:38:40.836
I don't know if that's true.

553
00:38:40.862 --> 00:38:43.099
So they lied to me?

554
00:38:43.123 --> 00:38:44.005
Who?

555
00:38:44.030 --> 00:38:48.346
My friends, they're liars.
You're not Potato Chip?

556
00:38:48.371 --> 00:38:49.943
Sorry.

557
00:38:51.900 --> 00:38:55.273
I can't really hear you.
Can we move?

558
00:38:55.298 --> 00:38:56.996
Yeah.

559
00:38:58.297 --> 00:38:59.916
Where...

560
00:39:08.291 --> 00:39:10.614
What were you babbling about?

561
00:39:10.639 --> 00:39:11.465
Nice. Um...

562
00:39:11.489 --> 00:39:13.130
Jake Davis,

563
00:39:13.155 --> 00:39:18.297
he wrote my favorite book,
of all time, "Fathers and Daughters".

564
00:39:19.039 --> 00:39:21.628
Wow. It's a popular book?

565
00:39:21.652 --> 00:39:22.641
Yeah.

566
00:39:22.666 --> 00:39:26.882
I know. It's just been with me
ever since I was a little kid.

567
00:39:26.907 --> 00:39:28.556
It...

568
00:39:28.581 --> 00:39:32.021
literally changed my life. So...

569
00:39:32.297 --> 00:39:35.481
Hi. My name's Cameron.

570
00:39:35.833 --> 00:39:38.092
I'm Katie.

571
00:39:39.081 --> 00:39:40.628
Katie?

572
00:39:40.653 --> 00:39:41.688
Yes.

573
00:39:41.713 --> 00:39:45.184
As in, "Kate Davis"?

574
00:39:49.865 --> 00:39:52.043
You're the real Kate Davis?

575
00:39:53.699 --> 00:39:57.746
How close is the book to what
actually happened?

576
00:39:57.771 --> 00:39:59.989
It's a lot funnier in the book.

577
00:40:00.014 --> 00:40:00.972
Okay.

578
00:40:01.920 --> 00:40:06.306
Is this your thing?
You go out, alone, no friends?

579
00:40:06.331 --> 00:40:08.512
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

580
00:40:08.538 --> 00:40:11.398
Sometimes I really just...
I prefer being alone.

581
00:40:11.422 --> 00:40:13.996
It's a lot easier.

582
00:40:14.998 --> 00:40:17.371
So what do you do?

583
00:40:18.346 --> 00:40:22.500
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLES)</font> I'm a social worker.
I work with kids with problems.

584
00:40:23.211 --> 00:40:25.297
- Wow.
- Yeah.

585
00:40:25.322 --> 00:40:26.804
I like it.

586
00:40:30.385 --> 00:40:32.431
So how do you get by?

587
00:40:32.456 --> 00:40:35.596
I'm a freelance writer
for a few newspapers

588
00:40:35.621 --> 00:40:39.344
and starting my first book.

589
00:40:39.717 --> 00:40:41.653
What's it called?

590
00:40:41.679 --> 00:40:44.097
- You really wanna know?
- Yeah.

591
00:40:44.121 --> 00:40:47.628
Uh... "Two is the Perfect Number."

592
00:40:48.489 --> 00:40:50.889
- Two is the Perfect Number?
- Yeah.

593
00:40:50.914 --> 00:40:52.699
Is that a love story?

594
00:40:52.724 --> 00:40:56.726
Uh... Yeah. Kind of.

595
00:40:58.692 --> 00:41:00.693
This is me.

596
00:41:00.719 --> 00:41:02.434
- This is you.
- Yeah.

597
00:41:02.460 --> 00:41:05.320
Wow, this is really nice!

598
00:41:05.344 --> 00:41:07.684
Perfect for a Potato Chip.

599
00:41:08.226 --> 00:41:10.842
Well, you're never seeing
my apartment.

600
00:41:10.867 --> 00:41:18.588
I'm... well, not the would...
This is a... date or... anything but... uh

601
00:41:20.623 --> 00:41:23.195
What are you doing tomorrow?

602
00:41:23.827 --> 00:41:25.003
Why?

603
00:41:25.027 --> 00:41:29.224
Well, so we can continue
this conversation.

604
00:41:31.181 --> 00:41:34.284
I was, you know, running.

605
00:41:34.309 --> 00:41:35.873
I can run.

606
00:41:36.831 --> 00:41:39.864
- Would you like to join me?
- Yeah, I would.

607
00:41:39.889 --> 00:41:41.436
Okay.

608
00:41:42.809 --> 00:41:44.414
Um...

609
00:41:44.670 --> 00:41:46.610
Meet me up here at four.

610
00:41:46.635 --> 00:41:49.251
Four? Okay.

611
00:41:50.996 --> 00:41:53.416
Um... Sweet... Sweet dreams.

612
00:41:54.623 --> 00:41:57.313
Sweet dreams to you too,
Cameron.

613
00:42:00.943 --> 00:42:02.927
- Good night.
- <font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> Night.

614
00:42:13.443 --> 00:42:17.599
<font color="#808080">JAKE:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(NARRATING)</font> The rising
moon draws the youthful eye,

615
00:42:17.623 --> 00:42:21.715
rising and shining,
full of grace and hope.

616
00:42:21.740 --> 00:42:26.476
Yes, the tulips are beautiful,
for now.

617
00:42:28.373 --> 00:42:33.985
Everything lives and dies,
rises and falls,

618
00:42:34.731 --> 00:42:37.407
and loves and leaves...

619
00:42:40.005 --> 00:42:43.519
<font color="#D900D9">(CROWD APPLAUDING)</font>

620
00:42:52.436 --> 00:42:55.231
You can pre-order
"Bitter tulips" downstairs.

621
00:42:55.255 --> 00:43:00.349
And Mr. Davis is also graciously agreed to
sign copies of his previous books,

622
00:43:00.373 --> 00:43:04.485
which we've conveniently made
available to you. Thank you.

623
00:43:04.487 --> 00:43:06.500
<font color="#D900D9">(CROWD CONTINUES APPLAUDING)</font>

624
00:43:12.005 --> 00:43:13.454
<font color="#D900D9">(CROWD CHATTERING)</font>

625
00:43:13.456 --> 00:43:14.800
Kerri.

626
00:43:14.826 --> 00:43:15.541
<font color="#808080">JAKE:</font> With a C?

627
00:43:15.567 --> 00:43:16.675
- With a K.
- Okay.

628
00:43:16.699 --> 00:43:19.030
K-E-R-R-I.

629
00:43:24.110 --> 00:43:25.378
K...

630
00:43:25.403 --> 00:43:27.844
K-E-R-R-I.

631
00:43:30.623 --> 00:43:31.813
Thank you!

632
00:43:37.541 --> 00:43:39.496
Make it out "To Nancy".

633
00:43:59.831 --> 00:44:01.255
I need a minute.

634
00:44:01.896 --> 00:44:03.307
Just a minute.

635
00:44:06.074 --> 00:44:07.213
Just a minute.

636
00:44:13.715 --> 00:44:15.030
Excuse me.

637
00:44:16.599 --> 00:44:17.742
Excuse me.

638
00:44:20.666 --> 00:44:21.893
Excuse me.

639
00:44:33.050 --> 00:44:35.320
<font color="#D900D9">(RATTLING, THUDDING)</font>

640
00:44:48.706 --> 00:44:50.715
Mr. Davis, are you all right?

641
00:44:52.005 --> 00:44:55.400
<font color="#D900D9">(JAKE PANTING, MOANS)</font>

642
00:44:55.590 --> 00:44:57.275
Mr. Davis?

643
00:44:58.916 --> 00:45:00.219
It's alright.

644
00:45:07.099 --> 00:45:09.320
<font color="#D900D9">("WALTZ" PLAYING)</font>

645
00:45:18.123 --> 00:45:19.802
Is this how a princess dances?

646
00:45:19.826 --> 00:45:22.980
Yes, it is.
Exactly how a princess dances.

647
00:45:23.005 --> 00:45:28.679
It's called waltz. And when you're a little
bit older, I'll show you how to do it.

648
00:45:29.576 --> 00:45:33.284
So if I'm a princess,
Am I gonna meet a prince one day?

649
00:45:33.309 --> 00:45:34.556
Yeah, absolutely.

650
00:45:34.581 --> 00:45:35.836
When? When?

651
00:45:35.862 --> 00:45:39.365
I don't know when.
When the time is right.

652
00:45:39.391 --> 00:45:40.965
What's his name gonna be?

653
00:45:40.990 --> 00:45:43.706
His name is gonna be...

654
00:45:43.731 --> 00:45:45.074
- Prince something.
- <font color="#D900D9">(BOTH LAUGHS)</font>

655
00:45:46.425 --> 00:45:48.534
I don't know what
his name's gonna be.

656
00:46:01.005 --> 00:46:03.230
<font color="#D900D9">(INAUDIBLE DIALOGUE)</font>

657
00:46:37.166 --> 00:46:41.851
This guy is saying ten years from now
everyone will write on computers.

658
00:46:42.208 --> 00:46:45.188
The typewriter will go the way of
the horse and buggy.

659
00:46:45.213 --> 00:46:46.184
Ass.

660
00:46:47.945 --> 00:46:50.911
Jake, some of the reviews
of the Tulips have come in.

661
00:46:50.936 --> 00:46:51.900
Yeah?

662
00:46:54.039 --> 00:46:55.045
Bad?

663
00:46:58.148 --> 00:47:02.925
A book so bad it makes you wonder
if Jake Davis was really ever that good.

664
00:47:03.331 --> 00:47:04.518
Oh.

665
00:47:06.541 --> 00:47:07.900
This is awful.

666
00:47:07.925 --> 00:47:09.795
Well, you've had bad reviews before.

667
00:47:09.820 --> 00:47:13.003
Yeah, but not like this. This is just...
personal attack.

668
00:47:13.027 --> 00:47:14.108
It's...

669
00:47:14.132 --> 00:47:16.123
This is uh...

670
00:47:17.081 --> 00:47:18.782
No.

671
00:47:18.807 --> 00:47:20.317
It's a...

672
00:47:20.342 --> 00:47:22.317
There's got to be others, right?

673
00:47:23.088 --> 00:47:25.498
- He just didn't get it.
- No.

674
00:47:25.775 --> 00:47:29.978
So incomprehensible. All that matters
might as well be written in aramaic.

675
00:47:30.003 --> 00:47:31.717
Or better yet not at all.

676
00:47:33.005 --> 00:47:35.420
<font color="#D900D9">(CLEARS THROAT, LAUGHS)</font>

677
00:47:37.407 --> 00:47:39.092
I've had better times

678
00:47:40.230 --> 00:47:41.277
Who wrote it?

679
00:47:41.302 --> 00:47:42.184
Colson.

680
00:47:43.208 --> 00:47:44.864
- He's just a little prick, right?
- Yeah.

681
00:47:44.889 --> 00:47:46.525
I wouldn't do the blurb for his novella.

682
00:47:46.550 --> 00:47:48.369
See? He's just getting some revenge.

683
00:47:48.393 --> 00:47:50.610
Knopf's gonna cut initial run in half.

684
00:47:50.635 --> 00:47:56.931
But I mean if it starts to sell what, marketing,
I think they're probably gonna cut that too.

685
00:47:56.956 --> 00:47:59.309
Well, if they don't support us,
it's just dead in the water.

686
00:47:59.333 --> 00:48:02.346
What can I...
If they are not paying for ads,

687
00:48:02.371 --> 00:48:05.454
if they're not putting a platform,
I can't do anything.

688
00:48:05.478 --> 00:48:06.864
I fought like a bastard.

689
00:48:06.889 --> 00:48:08.688
They do not care
what you have done.

690
00:48:08.713 --> 00:48:10.519
Just a bunch of bean counters.

691
00:48:11.063 --> 00:48:13.030
They're just reviews.

692
00:48:13.056 --> 00:48:15.103
It's just you know...

693
00:48:15.128 --> 00:48:17.527
- I don't care about reviews
- Right.

694
00:48:17.552 --> 00:48:19.226
All right. I'll see you later.

695
00:48:20.010 --> 00:48:23.230
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

696
00:48:26.005 --> 00:48:28.230
- <font color="#D900D9">(SIREN WAILING IN DISTANCE)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(DRILLING IN DISTANT)</font>

697
00:48:40.813 --> 00:48:43.416
<font color="#D900D9">(SINGSONGY)</font>
An arm, two arms...

698
00:48:43.534 --> 00:48:45.369
- You know...
- Mm-hmm?

699
00:48:45.394 --> 00:48:49.083
If you don't wanna go to
aunt Elizabeth's birthday,

700
00:48:49.108 --> 00:48:51.182
you don't have to, you know.

701
00:48:51.610 --> 00:48:54.411
I know, but I wanna go.

702
00:48:54.436 --> 00:48:55.681
- Really?
- Yep.

703
00:48:55.706 --> 00:49:00.418
Because we could go and do something else,
like anything you want.

704
00:49:00.443 --> 00:49:02.641
But daddy, I wanna go.

705
00:49:03.045 --> 00:49:04.545
- Really?
- Yep.

706
00:49:04.750 --> 00:49:07.804
- Is bribery gonna work? No?
- No.

707
00:49:11.780 --> 00:49:13.505
You look beautiful.

708
00:49:13.530 --> 00:49:14.650
Thank you.

709
00:49:15.090 --> 00:49:17.420
- <font color="#D900D9">(PIANO PLAYING)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(CHATTERING)</font>

710
00:49:18.956 --> 00:49:20.206
<font color="#808080">ELIZABETH:</font> Katie!

711
00:49:21.251 --> 00:49:23.132
Hi!

712
00:49:23.134 --> 00:49:25.052
<font color="#D900D9">(LAUGHING)</font>

713
00:49:25.054 --> 00:49:26.561
Finally!

714
00:49:26.585 --> 00:49:28.786
I missed you so much!

715
00:49:28.811 --> 00:49:30.748
Look who's here, kids!

716
00:50:00.007 --> 00:50:01.487
<font color="#808080">WILLIAM:</font> Jake.

717
00:50:01.512 --> 00:50:02.639
William.

718
00:50:03.259 --> 00:50:04.905
Ah, thanks for coming.

719
00:50:05.302 --> 00:50:07.447
I'm sorry. I hear about your book.

720
00:50:07.472 --> 00:50:10.849
It must've been rough the way
the criticism pegged down to you.

721
00:50:10.873 --> 00:50:13.181
Yeah, well, you know...

722
00:50:13.206 --> 00:50:17.641
I don't know why God invented cockroaches
or literary critics. I'm sure he had his reasons.

723
00:50:17.666 --> 00:50:19.778
Well, you know, I mean,
they just hated it.

724
00:50:19.804 --> 00:50:22.731
I mean, they actively hated it.
How do you get passed on like that?

725
00:50:22.755 --> 00:50:26.077
Well, you know, pick a cellphone,
the self-affluent.

726
00:50:26.103 --> 00:50:27.619
That kind of thing.

727
00:50:29.333 --> 00:50:33.797
You know, have you even noticed...

728
00:50:33.822 --> 00:50:35.199
that you're shaking.

729
00:50:35.224 --> 00:50:38.831
The last time we met, it looked to me like
you were about to have a seizure.

730
00:50:38.856 --> 00:50:39.601
And I... I admit,

731
00:50:39.626 --> 00:50:44.989
I mean I was disturbed to see you still
wrestling with an impulses you can't control

732
00:50:45.014 --> 00:50:47.826
even after all that time
in the hospital.

733
00:50:47.851 --> 00:50:50.431
The book's prove, Jake.

734
00:50:50.456 --> 00:50:53.336
You're not ready for the real world.
You're not cut out to be a father.

735
00:50:53.362 --> 00:50:57.271
You just give Katie to somebody
actually can take care of her.

736
00:50:57.295 --> 00:51:00.034
Tell your kid that you love her,
and then you can't do what's best for her.

737
00:51:00.067 --> 00:51:01.594
That's hypocrisy at the worst.

738
00:51:03.005 --> 00:51:06.519
- <font color="#D900D9">(CHATTERING STOPS)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(WILLIAM CHUCKLES)</font>

739
00:51:06.994 --> 00:51:09.106
Carl, just not so much left-hand.

740
00:51:11.307 --> 00:51:13.708
That's funny, man.
That's funny.

741
00:51:14.894 --> 00:51:17.164
You're in deep shit now.

742
00:51:23.061 --> 00:51:24.476
Nice move.

743
00:51:25.130 --> 00:51:27.237
You'd better mind.
He's mannerless.

744
00:51:47.090 --> 00:51:50.420
<font color="#D900D9">(WINCES, GROANS)</font>

745
00:52:03.206 --> 00:52:06.498
<font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> Daddy, Sit here
and read me a book!

746
00:52:06.713 --> 00:52:10.666
Yeah, baby.
I'll be right there.

747
00:52:17.050 --> 00:52:19.230
<font color="#D900D9">(TYPEWRITER KEYS CLACKING)</font>

748
00:52:36.878 --> 00:52:39.706
Oh, shit! Shit! Shit!

749
00:52:49.818 --> 00:52:50.998
Katie, your dad's here.

750
00:52:51.023 --> 00:52:52.215
Hey!

751
00:52:52.791 --> 00:52:56.157
Sorry. The train got stuck
at Park Street Station.

752
00:52:56.188 --> 00:52:58.842
Somebody pulled
the emergency ring. Hey.

753
00:52:58.867 --> 00:53:01.240
You said you would set the alarm
when you're working!

754
00:53:01.266 --> 00:53:03.628
I hate being the last one picked up!

755
00:53:04.331 --> 00:53:05.940
Potato Chip.

756
00:53:05.965 --> 00:53:07.726
Hey.

757
00:53:16.902 --> 00:53:20.666
There seems to be a very
grumpy child here.

758
00:53:20.690 --> 00:53:26.179
Trying to take away the grumpiness
one layer at a time.

759
00:53:28.748 --> 00:53:30.592
Okay.

760
00:53:30.617 --> 00:53:33.023
Yeah, that's a little bit
of grumpiness gone.

761
00:53:34.846 --> 00:53:37.461
I still see some grumpiness.

762
00:53:41.697 --> 00:53:43.833
Gone! It's all gone.

763
00:53:43.858 --> 00:53:45.898
Here I'm a pretty good doctor.

764
00:53:46.715 --> 00:53:49.032
<font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> Okay.
I'll stay with you, okay?

765
00:53:49.938 --> 00:53:53.536
All right, I'm gonna give you a big push
and let you go, okay?

766
00:53:54.143 --> 00:53:55.170
Go!

767
00:53:55.195 --> 00:53:56.476
Go! Go!

768
00:53:56.501 --> 00:53:57.360
Go, Lucy!

769
00:53:57.385 --> 00:54:00.340
Yes! Go, keep going, Lucy. Go!

770
00:54:08.259 --> 00:54:11.342
That's my girl!

771
00:54:18.442 --> 00:54:22.509
<font color="#808080">CAMERON:</font> You wanna know what
made me decide to become a writer?

772
00:54:22.534 --> 00:54:24.056
Really stick to it?

773
00:54:24.480 --> 00:54:26.557
Well, when I was in Kenya,

774
00:54:26.583 --> 00:54:31.547
one morning I woke up
and jumped out of the car, to pee,

775
00:54:31.572 --> 00:54:34.724
and... I was face to face with a lion.

776
00:54:35.184 --> 00:54:36.322
Really?

777
00:54:36.347 --> 00:54:37.806
Yeah, I know, for real.

778
00:54:37.831 --> 00:54:40.869
I mean, a male lion
about 15 feet in front of me

779
00:54:40.894 --> 00:54:43.728
just staring straight at me.

780
00:54:43.753 --> 00:54:47.570
I mean, he was clearly telling me
that I was his.

781
00:54:47.594 --> 00:54:49.059
What'd you do?

782
00:54:49.083 --> 00:54:50.820
I didn't do anything.
I was frozen.

783
00:54:50.846 --> 00:54:53.704
I mean, I physically could not move.

784
00:54:54.141 --> 00:54:57.463
You know, he stared at me for
a few more moments and he just...

785
00:54:57.487 --> 00:55:00.440
walked right past me.

786
00:55:01.588 --> 00:55:04.940
I will never forget that moment,
you know.

787
00:55:04.965 --> 00:55:09.570
I realized that no more plan B,

788
00:55:09.594 --> 00:55:13.025
no documentary, no veterinarian,

789
00:55:13.050 --> 00:55:15.338
no Harvard.

790
00:55:15.362 --> 00:55:18.748
I just wanted to do what
I always dreamed of, you know?

791
00:55:18.773 --> 00:55:22.143
I wanted to write, you know?

792
00:55:22.168 --> 00:55:28.543
I wanted to write as if every page I was writing on
was the last page before I die.

793
00:55:28.568 --> 00:55:29.990
You know? I wanna...

794
00:55:30.016 --> 00:55:32.163
I wanna leave something behind.

795
00:55:32.188 --> 00:55:34.009
You know? I wanna...

796
00:55:34.034 --> 00:55:37.945
I wanna leave my mark,
because you know what,

797
00:55:37.969 --> 00:55:47.262
sooner or later, in one form or another,
a lion is just gonna come and get us all.

798
00:55:47.862 --> 00:55:50.626
I'm so glad that he let you live.

799
00:55:51.951 --> 00:55:54.235
Yeah, so am I.

800
00:55:57.112 --> 00:55:58.574
So am I.

801
00:57:19.755 --> 00:57:21.367
Coming to bed?

802
00:57:21.753 --> 00:57:23.992
- Yeah, in a bit.
- <font color="#D900D9">(KEYBOARD KEYS CLACKING)</font>

803
00:57:29.030 --> 00:57:31.144
I have something for you.

804
00:57:31.170 --> 00:57:32.320
Hmm?

805
00:57:34.050 --> 00:57:35.177
What?

806
00:57:38.628 --> 00:57:40.588
What is this?

807
00:57:45.893 --> 00:57:47.583
It's the original.

808
00:57:53.266 --> 00:57:55.963
To Katie, My Potato Chip,

809
00:57:56.512 --> 00:58:00.474
who I love more
than the last number.

810
00:58:03.920 --> 00:58:06.425
Katie I can't accept this.

811
00:58:06.451 --> 00:58:08.059
I want you to have it.

812
00:58:11.885 --> 00:58:13.657
It's a good luck charm.

813
00:58:15.012 --> 00:58:16.300
It's for you.

814
00:58:32.449 --> 00:58:34.976
- You can't catch me.
- Yep.

815
00:58:35.001 --> 00:58:36.041
No, you can't.

816
00:58:36.067 --> 00:58:37.157
I'm on this side.

817
00:58:37.182 --> 00:58:40.021
- Well, I bet I can go faster than you.
- No, no. I'm on this side.

818
00:58:41.135 --> 00:58:42.094
I go faster than you.

819
00:58:42.119 --> 00:58:43.027
Come on then.

820
00:58:43.717 --> 00:58:44.547
Race.

821
00:58:44.572 --> 00:58:45.335
Okay!

822
00:58:47.856 --> 00:58:50.190
- Yeah! Up the bridge.
- Up the bridge.

823
00:58:51.056 --> 00:58:52.298
Come on!

824
00:58:54.483 --> 00:58:56.021
Daddy, wait!

825
00:58:56.230 --> 00:58:57.376
- Come on baby.
- <font color="#D900D9">(KATIE SHRIEKS)</font>

826
00:59:00.469 --> 00:59:02.079
Up the bridge.

827
00:59:05.021 --> 00:59:06.769
I got it!

828
00:59:07.052 --> 00:59:08.829
Right. Don't forget to round that.

829
00:59:08.855 --> 00:59:10.141
We're gonna go round the turn.

830
00:59:10.166 --> 00:59:11.478
- Okay.
- Here we go.

831
00:59:12.018 --> 00:59:13.467
Around the turn.

832
00:59:14.268 --> 00:59:15.523
And another time.

833
00:59:19.427 --> 00:59:24.302
I can't believe I have a daughter
who puts ketchup on a hot dog.

834
00:59:25.184 --> 00:59:26.659
You don't like ketchup?

835
00:59:27.309 --> 00:59:30.088
On hamburgers, on French fries.

836
00:59:30.112 --> 00:59:31.807
On a hot dog? Ridiculous.

837
00:59:32.320 --> 00:59:34.079
Well, I'm my own person.

838
00:59:35.101 --> 00:59:37.713
Yeah, you are.

839
00:59:38.166 --> 00:59:40.920
<font color="#808080">MEN:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(SINGING)</font>
Happy birthday!

840
00:59:42.005 --> 00:59:46.420
Happy birthday to you.
Happy birthday to you.

841
00:59:47.005 --> 00:59:49.420
Happy birthday. Dear, Katie.

842
00:59:52.005 --> 00:59:54.320
- Happy birthday to you!
- <font color="#D900D9">(KATIE LAUGHS)</font>

843
00:59:54.320 --> 00:59:56.400
<font color="#D900D9">(COSTUMERS APPLAUDING)</font>

844
00:59:57.260 --> 00:59:58.545
Thanks, guys.

845
00:59:58.894 --> 01:00:00.672
- Make a wish?
- Yeah.

846
01:00:05.172 --> 01:00:07.380
- Happy birthday, Katie!
- <font color="#D900D9">(CONTINUES APPLAUDING)</font>

847
01:00:08.956 --> 01:00:11.175
- Happy birthday, Potato Chip.
- I love you.

848
01:00:12.695 --> 01:00:15.744
Wow, look at those teeth.

849
01:00:16.688 --> 01:00:21.862
I bet you all the other dinosaurs didn't
wanna bump into this guy at dinner time.

850
01:00:36.088 --> 01:00:37.427
Miss your mom?

851
01:00:39.635 --> 01:00:40.742
Me too.

852
01:00:50.472 --> 01:00:51.784
Hey...

853
01:00:55.702 --> 01:01:00.018
You know you were the great joy
in light of your mom's life,

854
01:01:00.043 --> 01:01:03.260
just like you're the great
joy in light of mine.

855
01:01:04.918 --> 01:01:06.030
<font color="#D900D9">(CRYING)</font>
I really miss her.

856
01:01:06.054 --> 01:01:07.730
Ooh, of course you do.

857
01:01:07.913 --> 01:01:09.186
Of course you do.

858
01:01:10.460 --> 01:01:12.027
But you know what?

859
01:01:12.052 --> 01:01:15.295
Your mom is wherever you are.

860
01:01:16.833 --> 01:01:18.539
She's in this room right now.

861
01:01:18.565 --> 01:01:19.807
She's watching over us.

862
01:01:19.833 --> 01:01:21.271
She's looking down.

863
01:01:21.297 --> 01:01:24.646
She's got a big smile on her face
and she's so proud.

864
01:01:24.670 --> 01:01:26.952
She's so proud of you baby.

865
01:01:26.978 --> 01:01:32.170
'cause she can see the intelligent,
caring, beautiful little girl you are.

866
01:01:33.643 --> 01:01:34.577
Yeah.

867
01:01:36.474 --> 01:01:37.646
Baby.

868
01:01:39.266 --> 01:01:41.221
Are you going to die?

869
01:01:43.481 --> 01:01:44.860
Not for a very very long time,

870
01:01:44.885 --> 01:01:47.490
when I'm an old old old man.

871
01:01:47.896 --> 01:01:49.297
How old?

872
01:01:49.797 --> 01:01:52.565
Well, probably about...

873
01:01:52.590 --> 01:01:53.568
a thousand.

874
01:01:53.594 --> 01:01:54.472
Yeah.

875
01:01:54.498 --> 01:01:57.434
Yeah. Maybe a million,
if I stop eating hot dogs.

876
01:01:57.713 --> 01:01:59.666
Daddy?

877
01:02:00.505 --> 01:02:05.123
I will be such an old man, all right?

878
01:02:05.148 --> 01:02:07.655
You'll have your own house
and your own husband.

879
01:02:07.681 --> 01:02:08.932
You'll have a whole
bunch of kids.

880
01:02:08.958 --> 01:02:10.682
You'll have a dog and a cat

881
01:02:10.708 --> 01:02:13.795
and everybody will be running around
putting ketch-up on everything.

882
01:02:19.318 --> 01:02:20.675
Promise.

883
01:02:22.476 --> 01:02:23.768
I promise.

884
01:02:24.101 --> 01:02:26.313
Pinky swear?

885
01:02:29.347 --> 01:02:30.918
Pinky swear.

886
01:02:38.402 --> 01:02:39.695
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font> Jake Davis?

887
01:02:40.501 --> 01:02:41.539
Yeah.

888
01:02:42.679 --> 01:02:44.474
You've been served.

889
01:02:50.391 --> 01:02:53.289
I have to admit I was shocked
when Bob shared your case with me.

890
01:02:53.315 --> 01:02:57.157
It's unprecedented for an aunt and uncle
to sue for the custody of their niece

891
01:02:57.182 --> 01:03:00.378
when the biological father
is not only alive and well.

892
01:03:01.088 --> 01:03:02.514
The famous author of The Boot.

893
01:03:02.539 --> 01:03:06.407
Jake, John Wilton is the best
custody lawyer in the country.

894
01:03:06.432 --> 01:03:09.519
I can't tell you how happy
I am he sent us your case.

895
01:03:09.545 --> 01:03:15.137
Sometimes these cases more about hurt feelings
than a geniune desire to obtain custody.

896
01:03:16.184 --> 01:03:20.581
First step is for you to sit down with William,
try and talk him out of pursuing this.

897
01:03:21.465 --> 01:03:23.237
And if he refuses to drop it?

898
01:03:23.262 --> 01:03:25.295
We'll file a motion to dismiss,

899
01:03:25.320 --> 01:03:27.581
argue the case is completely without merit.

900
01:03:28.369 --> 01:03:29.750
And if that fails?

901
01:03:30.416 --> 01:03:31.942
We'll kick their ass in court.

902
01:03:47.512 --> 01:03:48.521
Jake.

903
01:03:48.545 --> 01:03:49.597
Scotch, neat.

904
01:03:49.623 --> 01:03:50.740
<font color="#808080">WAITER:</font> Right away, sir.

905
01:03:59.998 --> 01:04:01.217
I'll start.

906
01:04:02.570 --> 01:04:06.932
Look, I want you to know it's
not a vendetta against you.

907
01:04:08.132 --> 01:04:10.128
We don't blame you for
what happened to Patricia

908
01:04:10.152 --> 01:04:13.750
and we're not retaliating
because you kept Katie

909
01:04:13.751 --> 01:04:17.699
away from us after we took care
of her for a year in your absence.

910
01:04:18.795 --> 01:04:22.101
Our only concern is Katie's welfare.

911
01:04:23.565 --> 01:04:27.248
And if you asked her, she tells you in a
heartbeat she wants to stay with me?

912
01:04:27.273 --> 01:04:28.601
Well, she's eight.

913
01:04:30.456 --> 01:04:32.277
It's inadmissible in court.

914
01:04:32.704 --> 01:04:34.210
It still matters.

915
01:04:35.507 --> 01:04:37.478
You're a reasonable man, William.

916
01:04:38.434 --> 01:04:39.889
And you're a father.

917
01:04:42.539 --> 01:04:46.050
I know that in your heart you
know what you're doing is wrong.

918
01:04:46.818 --> 01:04:53.088
Now I admit, I was angry
when I came to pick up Katie

919
01:04:53.112 --> 01:04:56.237
and you talked of adopting her
out from under me.

920
01:04:57.003 --> 01:05:01.838
And perhaps, at the party
I overreacted.

921
01:05:03.317 --> 01:05:06.023
Perhaps, you overreacted?

922
01:05:07.119 --> 01:05:10.097
I'm truly sorry for what
happened at Elizabeth's party.

923
01:05:10.838 --> 01:05:12.335
You provoked me,

924
01:05:12.360 --> 01:05:15.418
but that still doesn't
justify my action.

925
01:05:15.443 --> 01:05:23.041
And I would welcome
you and Elizabeth

926
01:05:23.067 --> 01:05:25.425
being more involved
in Katie's life.

927
01:05:25.449 --> 01:05:27.204
Jake, I...

928
01:05:28.360 --> 01:05:31.422
Hey, I didn't file the lawsuit
as a bargaining chip.

929
01:05:32.090 --> 01:05:34.164
You know my lawyer John Wilton.

930
01:05:34.773 --> 01:05:36.206
He's a great attorney.

931
01:05:36.900 --> 01:05:38.190
He's not cheap.

932
01:05:39.003 --> 01:05:41.034
He tells me you
don't have a shot.

933
01:05:41.797 --> 01:05:47.025
He tells me they'll never separate a
daughter from her sole biological parent.

934
01:05:48.590 --> 01:05:50.429
You know you're gonna
lose, why do this?

935
01:05:50.454 --> 01:05:53.429
You spent a year in a mental institution
which did nothing

936
01:05:53.429 --> 01:05:55.559
to relieve you of your
psychotic breaks.

937
01:05:56.454 --> 01:06:02.161
3 dozen people witnessed you attack me
in my home at a birthday party

938
01:06:02.186 --> 01:06:04.489
'cause I didn't like your last book.

939
01:06:05.356 --> 01:06:08.398
You gave testimony to the Connecticut
state police that you were having

940
01:06:08.398 --> 01:06:12.422
a heated argument and speeding
at the time of your wife's death

941
01:06:12.422 --> 01:06:14.349
and while they didn't charge you
with reckless endangerment

942
01:06:14.351 --> 01:06:18.500
that is how it's gonna appear
to the custody judge.

943
01:06:20.074 --> 01:06:21.831
Your last book tanked,

944
01:06:21.856 --> 01:06:24.423
critically and commercially,
putting into doubt

945
01:06:24.425 --> 01:06:27.719
whether or not you can even
provide for Katie.

946
01:06:28.235 --> 01:06:30.963
And I've got a feeling
you're running out of money.

947
01:06:32.159 --> 01:06:35.496
But I'll know soon enough when I
subpoena you for national records.

948
01:06:39.434 --> 01:06:41.612
I got more money than God.

949
01:06:41.637 --> 01:06:44.277
If we lose, we'll appeal.

950
01:06:44.302 --> 01:06:47.543
If we lose the appeal,
we'll appeal that.

951
01:06:50.987 --> 01:06:54.420
How are you positioned to handle
a prolonged legal battle?

952
01:06:57.159 --> 01:06:59.896
You are a very good
lawyer, William.

953
01:07:01.668 --> 01:07:04.135
I'm trying to be a
very good uncle.

954
01:07:05.835 --> 01:07:09.317
No, what you're trying to do?

955
01:07:09.342 --> 01:07:12.398
Is you're trying to separate
a little girl

956
01:07:12.423 --> 01:07:15.847
who's already suffering deeply
from the loss of her mother,

957
01:07:15.871 --> 01:07:18.271
away from the father she loves

958
01:07:18.295 --> 01:07:20.012
and who loves her.

959
01:07:20.601 --> 01:07:23.135
That is what you're trying to do.

960
01:07:25.273 --> 01:07:28.987
I would hope there's a special place in hell
for somebody who would do that.

961
01:07:30.050 --> 01:07:32.682
<font color="#D900D9">(CAMERON & KATIE LAUGHING)</font>

962
01:07:32.684 --> 01:07:34.715
That did not actually happen!

963
01:07:35.335 --> 01:07:36.588
- No, impossible.
- Yes, it did.

964
01:07:36.614 --> 01:07:37.967
- Really?
- Yes.

965
01:07:38.699 --> 01:07:39.728
Wow.

966
01:07:40.545 --> 01:07:41.543
- We need a drink.
