- Yeah.

1220
01:25:34.194 --> 01:25:37.123
Okay, I'm gonna wash up.

1221
01:25:43.050 --> 01:25:45.319
<font color="#D900D9">(KATIE PANTING)</font>

1222
01:26:25.005 --> 01:26:28.420
<font color="#D900D9">(SNIFFLES, SIGHS)</font>

1223
01:26:51.032 --> 01:26:52.345
What is this?

1224
01:26:53.940 --> 01:26:55.212
What is this?

1225
01:26:57.938 --> 01:26:59.659
Katie, what is this?

1226
01:27:02.755 --> 01:27:05.289
Why would...
Why would you do this?

1227
01:27:06.795 --> 01:27:07.795
Katie!

1228
01:27:09.774 --> 01:27:12.016
You wanna, you wanna...
how is that... with this?

1229
01:27:12.497 --> 01:27:16.323
Hey, hey here, you're out.
You're out, you're out!

1230
01:27:25.431 --> 01:27:26.954
I don't want out.

1231
01:27:28.353 --> 01:27:29.899
- I don't want out.
- Get off.

1232
01:27:31.259 --> 01:27:32.564
Listen to me, please.

1233
01:27:33.497 --> 01:27:35.203
I don't know why I did that.

1234
01:27:35.228 --> 01:27:36.925
I... Please just listen to me.

1235
01:27:36.949 --> 01:27:37.699
Get off of me.

1236
01:27:37.725 --> 01:27:39.759
But... Cameron, please just
look at me, please!

1237
01:27:39.783 --> 01:27:41.324
Please, please, just look at me.

1238
01:27:41.356 --> 01:27:42.658
I...

1239
01:27:42.681 --> 01:27:44.920
I don't know why I did that.

1240
01:27:44.945 --> 01:27:46.274
I...

1241
01:27:46.810 --> 01:27:47.722
Just...

1242
01:27:47.747 --> 01:27:51.197
Just give me a second to
explain myself please.

1243
01:27:55.914 --> 01:27:57.368
Please I'm so scared.

1244
01:27:57.394 --> 01:27:58.774
Of what Katie?

1245
01:27:58.798 --> 01:28:00.608
Of what?
What are you so afraid of?

1246
01:28:00.632 --> 01:28:01.467
What?

1247
01:28:01.493 --> 01:28:02.273
Tell me what?

1248
01:28:02.297 --> 01:28:03.882
Of us!

1249
01:28:03.908 --> 01:28:06.896
You know what, I'm really trying
to understand you.

1250
01:28:06.921 --> 01:28:10.220
Kate, I'm really trying
to give you all of my love,

1251
01:28:10.246 --> 01:28:14.029
but you know I can't,
I can't do this anymore, okay?

1252
01:28:14.351 --> 01:28:16.413
Stop, just stop.

1253
01:28:16.439 --> 01:28:17.524
Please, Cameron.

1254
01:28:17.975 --> 01:28:19.122
Stop!

1255
01:28:21.725 --> 01:28:22.846
Wait.

1256
01:28:22.872 --> 01:28:24.601
Wait, please.

1257
01:28:24.627 --> 01:28:26.945
What did you think
would happen Kate?

1258
01:28:27.493 --> 01:28:28.250
What? Huh?

1259
01:28:28.787 --> 01:28:30.744
- Listen, I don't know how to do this.
- What? What?

1260
01:28:30.770 --> 01:28:31.728
What?

1261
01:28:31.752 --> 01:28:33.203
Do what? Do what?!

1262
01:28:33.592 --> 01:28:34.750
I'm sorry I made a mistake

1263
01:28:34.774 --> 01:28:35.685
You made a mistake?

1264
01:28:35.711 --> 01:28:37.948
You let some guy
come between your legs!

1265
01:28:37.972 --> 01:28:41.068
This's not a mistake, Kate!

1266
01:28:41.541 --> 01:28:43.386
All right? We're done!

1267
01:28:43.773 --> 01:28:46.261
We're done, stop, God!

1268
01:28:47.050 --> 01:28:52.079
- <font color="#D900D9">(KATIE SOBBING)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(STARTS ENGINE)</font>

1269
01:28:52.083 --> 01:28:53.131
Please!

1270
01:28:53.157 --> 01:28:54.088
Stop!

1271
01:28:55.050 --> 01:28:57.619
<font color="#D900D9">(TYRES SCREECHING)</font>

1272
01:28:58.050 --> 01:29:00.500
<font color="#D900D9">(SOBBING, SCREAMS)</font>
Oh, Shit!

1273
01:29:02.774 --> 01:29:04.149
Oh, no.

1274
01:30:20.649 --> 01:30:21.648
Hey.

1275
01:30:22.006 --> 01:30:25.646
You should come back
with me and Janine.

1276
01:30:27.050 --> 01:30:29.600
<font color="#D900D9">(MAN LAUGHING)</font>

1277
01:30:32.247 --> 01:30:33.448
I'd like that.

1278
01:30:34.050 --> 01:30:36.500
<font color="#D900D9">(JANINE LAUGHING)</font>
Cool. Let's go.

1279
01:30:39.479 --> 01:30:40.301
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font> Are you coming?

1280
01:30:40.327 --> 01:30:41.381
I'm coming.

1281
01:31:08.050 --> 01:31:09.560
<font color="#D900D9">("CLOSE TO YOU" PLAYING)</font>

1282
01:31:27.059 --> 01:31:28.003
Are you coming?

1283
01:31:28.029 --> 01:31:28.728
<font color="#D900D9">(SHOUTS)</font> Go!

1284
01:31:28.752 --> 01:31:29.689
Oh, okay.

1285
01:31:48.050 --> 01:31:50.500
<font color="#D900D9">(SOBBING)</font>

1286
01:31:59.347 --> 01:32:01.506
I miss you.

1287
01:32:17.194 --> 01:32:19.003
Can you call me a cab?

1288
01:32:32.007 --> 01:32:32.956
<font color="#808080">KATIE:</font> Hi.

1289
01:32:35.143 --> 01:32:36.033
Hey.

1290
01:32:37.779 --> 01:32:38.761
What're you doing up?

1291
01:32:38.786 --> 01:32:39.940
It's morning.

1292
01:32:40.663 --> 01:32:41.851
It's morning?

1293
01:32:50.484 --> 01:32:52.609
Could you read me just one book?

1294
01:32:59.908 --> 01:33:02.252
Why don't I read you all of them?

1295
01:33:06.853 --> 01:33:08.105
Hey.

1296
01:33:08.131 --> 01:33:09.706
You wanted to see me?

1297
01:33:13.704 --> 01:33:15.237
Well...

1298
01:33:16.220 --> 01:33:19.021
We have some...

1299
01:33:20.020 --> 01:33:21.854
We have some great news.

1300
01:33:22.497 --> 01:33:24.333
Lucy's leaving foster care.

1301
01:33:24.359 --> 01:33:25.947
She's been adopted.

1302
01:33:26.481 --> 01:33:27.162
Oh my god!

1303
01:33:27.186 --> 01:33:30.180
By a loving stable family in Queens.

1304
01:33:30.204 --> 01:33:32.682
They have two other children,
it's a perfect fit.

1305
01:33:33.184 --> 01:33:34.154
Queens?

1306
01:33:35.319 --> 01:33:37.926
Takes over an hour's subway to get here.

1307
01:33:38.475 --> 01:33:39.748
Uh...

1308
01:33:40.350 --> 01:33:41.484
Wow.

1309
01:33:41.947 --> 01:33:43.528
Look,

1310
01:33:47.845 --> 01:33:49.921
You can't see her anymore.

1311
01:33:52.882 --> 01:33:53.502
What?

1312
01:33:53.534 --> 01:33:58.725
She'll continue therapy with a social worker
who helps integrate her into her new community.

1313
01:33:58.750 --> 01:34:01.335
She needs a clean break from us.

1314
01:34:02.302 --> 01:34:03.547
You've done great work with her.

1315
01:34:03.573 --> 01:34:05.716
Honey, we're all very proud.

1316
01:34:06.472 --> 01:34:09.578
But, she can't start her new life
holding on to you.

1317
01:34:10.402 --> 01:34:12.197
This is standard procedure.

1318
01:34:12.842 --> 01:34:13.605
There's got to be a way...

1319
01:34:13.631 --> 01:34:17.555
This isn't like
taking Lucy to the park.

1320
01:34:19.086 --> 01:34:21.630
There's no way for me
to fudge this. I'm sorry.

1321
01:34:23.582 --> 01:34:26.868
Hey, this is great news.

1322
01:34:26.893 --> 01:34:29.219
This is what we hope and pray for.

1323
01:34:46.029 --> 01:34:48.502
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font> We have enough a lot
to talk about huh?

1324
01:34:51.350 --> 01:34:52.730
New family.

1325
01:34:54.090 --> 01:34:55.536
New school.

1326
01:35:04.099 --> 01:35:06.208
Everything's gonna be okay.

1327
01:35:08.737 --> 01:35:10.052
I promise.

1328
01:35:11.050 --> 01:35:13.500
- <font color="#D900D9">(SLAPS)</font>
- <font color="#D900D9">(GASPS)</font>

1329
01:35:27.039 --> 01:35:29.467
I don't remember
my mother much, but...

1330
01:35:29.493 --> 01:35:34.587
I love, love, love, my father.

1331
01:35:35.496 --> 01:35:36.724
He was a writer.

1332
01:35:37.487 --> 01:35:39.445
He was actually quite famous.

1333
01:35:40.426 --> 01:35:44.512
He wasn't so, uh... mentally,

1334
01:35:44.537 --> 01:35:46.890
but he stayed up all night every night,

1335
01:35:46.916 --> 01:35:48.898
finishing one last book.

1336
01:35:49.748 --> 01:35:51.573
That book was about me.

1337
01:35:53.180 --> 01:35:55.801
But really it was about life,

1338
01:35:55.826 --> 01:35:59.667
and how he never gave up on me.

1339
01:36:02.490 --> 01:36:06.112
It was his way of...

1340
01:36:06.136 --> 01:36:08.976
telling me how much he loved me.

1341
01:36:10.542 --> 01:36:12.313
And goodbye.

1342
01:36:13.881 --> 01:36:17.546
That's what this book
is really about. It's...

1343
01:36:18.220 --> 01:36:21.631
never ever give up.

1344
01:36:22.583 --> 01:36:29.947
Life's gonna be really
challenging and unfair,

1345
01:36:29.971 --> 01:36:33.588
and sometimes painful.

1346
01:36:34.202 --> 01:36:38.402
I mean, you've been through
a lot already,

1347
01:36:38.887 --> 01:36:44.432
but we can never give up
or stop moving forward or looking ahead,

1348
01:36:44.465 --> 01:36:49.077
no matter how hard the experiences
that we've been through are.

1349
01:36:53.306 --> 01:36:56.621
All I can do is tell you that.

1350
01:36:58.563 --> 01:37:00.020
I love you.

1351
01:37:02.190 --> 01:37:03.951
And goodbye.

1352
01:37:05.880 --> 01:37:07.190
I love you too.

1353
01:37:14.930 --> 01:37:16.900
<font color="#D900D9">(VOICE BREAKING)</font>
You be good, okay?

1354
01:37:18.082 --> 01:37:20.833
You have great things
in front of you.

1355
01:37:22.600 --> 01:37:23.850
I will.

1356
01:37:24.927 --> 01:37:26.367
I promise.

1357
01:37:44.226 --> 01:37:45.863
Congratulations, Jake.

1358
01:37:45.887 --> 01:37:46.847
What for?

1359
01:37:47.475 --> 01:37:48.957
You're gonna be an uncle again.

1360
01:37:48.981 --> 01:37:53.684
It seems your brother-in-law William
has been having an affair with his secretary.

1361
01:37:53.708 --> 01:37:54.831
Who's only 24.

1362
01:37:54.855 --> 01:37:56.474
And she's pregnant.

1363
01:37:56.498 --> 01:37:58.438
And she's keeping it.

1364
01:37:58.462 --> 01:38:00.734
Elizabeth's filing for divorce.

1365
01:38:01.198 --> 01:38:02.247
They dropped the suit.

1366
01:38:02.273 --> 01:38:04.149
- <font color="#808080">BOTH:</font> Oops!
- <font color="#D900D9">(BOTH LAUGHING)</font>

1367
01:38:11.005 --> 01:38:12.997
Fathers and Daughters.

1368
01:38:16.764 --> 01:38:22.463
How do you write a novel in three months?
Usually takes you years.

1369
01:38:24.537 --> 01:38:25.943
Is it any good?

1370
01:38:28.386 --> 01:38:29.574
No idea.

1371
01:38:31.957 --> 01:38:35.198
That's what you said to me when you
brought me Living the Dance.

1372
01:38:36.568 --> 01:38:38.059
I brought you what?

1373
01:38:40.829 --> 01:38:45.164
When you brought me Living the Dance,
the book you won the Pulitzer prize for.

1374
01:38:57.188 --> 01:38:58.534
Oh, God!

1375
01:39:46.050 --> 01:39:48.500
<font color="#D900D9">(GROANS)</font>

1376
01:39:58.050 --> 01:40:00.399
<font color="#D900D9">(CHOKING)</font>

1377
01:40:56.050 --> 01:40:58.600
<font color="#D900D9">(CROWS CAWING)</font>

1378
01:41:07.506 --> 01:41:10.703
Do you wanna say something
to your father?

1379
01:41:25.770 --> 01:41:27.761
You're my Potato Chip.

1380
01:41:29.561 --> 01:41:32.386
You and no one else.

1381
01:42:33.112 --> 01:42:34.756
Hi, sweetheart.

1382
01:43:12.050 --> 01:43:14.500
<font color="#D900D9">(RINGING)</font>

1383
01:44:45.050 --> 01:44:47.340
<font color="#D900D9">(PEOPLE CHATTERING)</font>

1384
01:45:20.050 --> 01:45:22.319
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS HEAVILY)</font>

1385
01:45:31.247 --> 01:45:32.207
- Hey.
- Hi.

1386
01:45:34.635 --> 01:45:35.920
I miss you.

1387
01:45:38.310 --> 01:45:39.600
And I love you.

1388
01:45:42.452 --> 01:45:44.694
God I love you so much.

1389
01:45:46.225 --> 01:45:48.625
I should've said it
a million times.

1390
01:45:48.649 --> 01:45:50.536
Yeah, I really should've.

1391
01:45:53.027 --> 01:45:55.728
I was so afraid of you leaving me.

1392
01:45:57.654 --> 01:46:01.466
And I know we both know
that I'm not easy.

1393
01:46:01.492 --> 01:46:03.104
I know I'm not.

1394
01:46:04.052 --> 01:46:05.404
And...

1395
01:46:07.693 --> 01:46:10.649
You're the best thing that
ever happened to me.

1396
01:46:11.586 --> 01:46:13.594
And you know what, I can't...

1397
01:46:14.041 --> 01:46:16.185
I don't wanna live without you.

1398
01:46:16.225 --> 01:46:20.216
<font color="#808080">WOMAN:</font>
Cameron, I can go.

1399
01:46:21.104 --> 01:46:24.189
It's my friend.

1400
01:46:28.868 --> 01:46:33.488
Thank you.
Thank you for everything.

1401
01:46:33.912 --> 01:46:34.951
Really.

1402
01:46:37.432 --> 01:46:38.487
Katie.

1403
01:46:40.001 --> 01:46:40.993
Katie.

1404
01:47:01.873 --> 01:47:09.106
It is a great honor to accept this Pulitzer
on behalf of my client, the late Jake Davis.

1405
01:47:09.131 --> 01:47:13.471
That Fathers and Daughters
has won every major literary award

1406
01:47:13.472 --> 01:47:16.496
and been perched to top
the best sellers' list for a year

1407
01:47:16.497 --> 01:47:19.399
is every agent's dream.

1408
01:47:21.024 --> 01:47:24.997
That I never got to buy Jake a drink
and slap him on the back

1409
01:47:25.021 --> 01:47:27.657
is my own personal nightmare.

1410
01:47:29.146 --> 01:47:33.069
Katie, I think you're the only person in the world
who will miss him more than I will.

1411
01:47:34.640 --> 01:47:36.926
- Thank you. Thank you.
- <font color="#D900D9">(CROWD APPLAUDING)</font>

1412
01:47:43.050 --> 01:47:46.500
<font color="#D900D9">(MUFFLED LAUGHING, CHATTERING)</font>

1413
01:48:02.774 --> 01:48:04.774
<font color="#808080">ELIZABETH:</font>
I've had a hard life.

1414
01:48:06.645 --> 01:48:11.206
I suppose I was hard right back.

1415
01:48:14.043 --> 01:48:17.292
I'm a grown woman
who's never known love.

1416
01:48:18.585 --> 01:48:20.275
Isn't that something?

1417
01:48:26.787 --> 01:48:29.078
My parents were just the same,

1418
01:48:29.103 --> 01:48:32.228
my mother was a terribly mean woman.

1419
01:48:33.323 --> 01:48:38.501
And my father, someone we saw
at the occasional Sunday dinner.

1420
01:48:41.511 --> 01:48:43.487
You know Katie.

1421
01:48:43.511 --> 01:48:45.810
Men...

1422
01:48:45.835 --> 01:48:48.635
...they can survive without love.

1423
01:48:50.733 --> 01:48:52.752
but not us women.

1424
01:49:36.570 --> 01:49:37.868
Come here.

1425
01:50:05.050 --> 01:50:40.666
<b><font color="#00FFFF">Subtitled By: Fidel33
